#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073461 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2b57f76-8fab-5b44-80ee-d905e5f9a14f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining How Many Parts Fit Into a Whole"}] :question/id #uuid "4f8f2348-c6ec-5073-9f95-6697173654a7" :question/math-academy-id "e-13690" :question/problem "![](images/46/4644be3ee3652c8a52d62e9d849d107e691dbf1f184ea247f02552af108b2e04.png)\n\nThe $3$ circles above are divided into halves. How many halves are there in total?" :question/worked-solution "Since each part is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}2}\n$$\n\nof a whole, we need to split each of the $\\color{red}3$ circles (wholes) into $\\color{blue}2$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e9/e92a0deb6d9542ca276fba5c7d17c64e45bad265dc8bd8dde2dce4fa166e3e89.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}3} \\times {\\color{blue}2} = 6\n$$\n\nparts in total."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073462 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed8053e5-f273-56f2-bfb6-294f936d9701" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Model Representing a Division Problem"}] :question/id #uuid "2f739b94-f494-546b-8623-bd17a525a436" :question/math-academy-id "e-13695" :question/problem "What model could represent the division problem below?\n$3 \\div \\dfrac{1}{6} = 18$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the following $\\color{red}3$ wholes:\n\n![](images/23/235e19c4e3231eb22e6d43ccadcd90c5694077ec4ce562e6c4f188cfff77545f.png)\n\nTo calculate\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}3} \\div \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}6}\n$$\n\n, we need to divide each of $\\color{red}3$ wholes into $\\color{blue}6$ equal parts, as shown below. This gives us the corresponding model for the given division problem.\n\n![](images/3b/3b3551ad59a9d5abe2bf03e350f373412959293c68a4f059123fafcbabf72936.png)\n\nWe get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}3} \\times {\\color{blue}6}= 18\n$$\n\npieces in total."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073467 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073722 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e33ab8e-736b-5972-af0d-f7eeabda1148" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Division Problem Represented by a Model"}] :question/id #uuid "dd5b4bc8-110c-5247-b5e6-ee4ce7636a1b" :question/math-academy-id "e-13707" :question/problem "Each of the three shapes in the model below represents one whole.\n\n![](images/22/222af9ec253a6624ece646225db926069cd7be3ac416fe846a9216360981f8cb.png)\n\nFrom left to right, what numbers are missing from the division problem below?\n$0$" :question/worked-solution "In the model, there are $\\color{red}3$ shapes. Each shape consists of $4$ pieces that each represent\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{4}\n$$\n\nof a whole. There are $\\color{blue}12$ pieces in total.\n\nThe model tells us that when we divide $\\color{red}3$ wholes into quarters, we will be left with $\\color{blue}12$ pieces.\n\nTherefore, the division problem is:\n$3$\n\nSo, the missing numbers are $\\color{red}3$ and $\\color{blue}12$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073468 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073723 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79e310e4-b8a2-5327-b4e6-fd71b6783e3a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Whole Numbers by Unit Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "06e730e3-2df3-5d28-afd1-72c34d11cf8e" :question/math-academy-id "e-13709" :question/problem "![](images/46/4644be3ee3652c8a52d62e9d849d107e691dbf1f184ea247f02552af108b2e04.png)\n\nThe model above represents $3$ wholes. Use this model to calculate the value of $3 \\div \\dfrac{1}{5}$." :question/worked-solution "To calculate\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}3} \\div \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}5}\n$$\n\n, we need to divide each of $\\color{red}3$ wholes into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/32/327833c4954c43c2093cb31a03cef01e66389e7cafc3bb2d4cd174e0f7e64f5d.png)\n\nWe get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}3} \\times {\\color{blue}5} = 15\n$$\n\npieces in total.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n3 \\div \\dfrac{1}{5} = 15\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074367 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ed8053e5-f273-56f2-bfb6-294f936d9701" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Model Representing a Division Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d56ceee-d053-5eea-a8b5-d2df8307e826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6f/6fabd67620c756d3369bea4e42d538443fa5dbf0cc3e6a84d1986e1691524da8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072441} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc94e94-ec11-56f3-b5cb-2476c1012b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d5/d5dcf87473aac113b98db49e37b9227da3d2467bc75e584b2d5e69bdcadf3513.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072442} {:answer/id #uuid "11f6c792-fd90-5828-825a-5e1c1258ea5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/92/9298eb33dbbe9cfc93712c86370ba589667f9512df85bece397733f85b48a8d7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072443} {:answer/id #uuid "4b10b130-8dd7-571f-8014-5b1b77a24f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/afb7294af7d3989a796daf94e9a995f00fb3303a71c8501e2d94caf05d0bce55.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072444} {:answer/id #uuid "60ed471e-297d-502b-a5a8-de28b97492f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c9/c9e54ff064fe956a8800c36764e5ee5b735f6d783a4255df29a8d3c980350fe8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072445}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9b38d868-1e61-5ac0-81ea-7185bfc30cd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186072440}] :question/id #uuid "6658ae40-945d-5a7e-bc48-40968bc45b17" :question/math-academy-id "q-59624" :question/problem "Which model represents the division problem below?\n$2 \\div \\frac{1}{5} = 10$"}]}
